+# Operational-record follow-up: witness, CIA, informant and drawing leads
+
+October 26, 2026. This additive public package publishes the eight RF findings
+from the operational-record follow-up and connects them to the later
+[bank/telephone integration](../bank-phone-integration-2026-10-26/README.md).
+The entry counts are not counts of independent corroborations or established
+conspiracies.
+
+The principal recovery is a complete six-page April 20, 2004 Commission
+interview memorandum. Its NARA-media and Commons copies match byte-for-byte.
+It contains both assistance-related observations and the witness's emphatic
+coincidence account. The report also preserves explicit alias associations,
+earlier witness-sequence questions, the party-video source trail, drawing-copy
+and custody references, and the distinction between aviation testimony and a
+court's preliminary inference about knowledge.
+
+Read the [full source review](REPORT.md), [eight qualified findings](findings.json),
+[source URLs, hashes and page locations](source-pins.json), and
+[current continuation](CURRENT.md). The historical [five-bundle targets](targets.json)
+remain unchanged; the [updated targets](../bank-phone-integration-2026-10-26/targets-v2.json)
+incorporate the published bank/telephone progress while retaining unresolved
+inputs and conflicting records.
+
+## Preserved records and publication status
+
+REPORT.md, RECORD.md, PROTOCOL.md, findings.json, targets.json and source-pins.json
+are exact copies of the preceding local study. Their local/unpublished wording
+records the status before the user's separate instruction to publish. It is
+preserved deliberately; this README and the publication scope record describe
+the subsequent publication. SOURCE-STUDY-MANIFEST.json inventories that earlier
+local study, not the public delivery set.
+
+Original PDFs, acquired response bodies, OCR and native-page images remain
+unchanged in local research holdings. They are not bulk-exported here, because
+some contain personal contact/account information. The public catalog retains
+source links, exact hashes and physical page references. Its relative holding
+locators identify the source study's files; they do not imply all raw files are
+present in this public package. No source, conflicting value or redaction was
+rewritten to make the publication cleaner.
+
+The NARA media acquisition receipt and Commons structured provenance are
+included under source-provenance/. Byte identity supports copy provenance; it
+does not independently establish every historical recollection. No scientific
+or historical reconstruction was performed for publication.
+
+## Open questions remain open
+
+The earlier witness interviews and complete litigation versions, original CIA
+draft/routing/delivery and oversight records, informant-payment purpose/voucher,
+complete notebook/copy/return records, and full expert/video exhibits remain
+targets. The bank/telephone integration supplies a narrow confirming carrier
+sample, not every missing bank or cellular original. The apartment-payment 1A
+lead does not close the separate $100,000 informant-payment inquiry.
+
+These records do not establish an attack-preparation operation, a WTC 7
+demolition link, or manufactured al-Qaeda attribution. Contrary evidence and
+alternative explanations are retained alongside the leads.
+
+The public file set is pinned by MANIFEST.json. Run the sibling integration's
+`python3 -B verify_publication.py` to check both packages and the retained
+bank/telephone snapshot. The verification covers bytes, links, recorded counts
+and coverage; it does not validate the historical hypotheses.
