+# Five operational-record bundles: witness recovery and evidentiary qualifications
+
+October26,2026. This is a new local tranche following the supplied S001-S014
+summary. The summary remains a claim/priority inventory. Newly obtained here
+means obtained in this pass, not newly discovered historical evidence.
+
+## Result
+
+The most substantial recovery is the **complete six-page April20,2004 Commission
+interview memorandum for Caysan Bin Don**, also naming Usama Dyson and Clayton
+Morgan. The Commons copy is byte-identical to the copy fetched from the NARA
+media endpoint identified in its structured archival metadata. This improves
+source provenance; it does not certify every recollection as historically true.
+
+A second newly acquired official record, **ECF11180, August28,2025**, places
+important qualifications on using aviation-expert opinions about Bayoumi's
+relationships and credibility while preserving technical testimony. It must be
+read beside ECF11182's substantive, preliminary jurisdictional inference about
+the drawing. Neither order independently supplies the original notebook or a
+final merits determination.
+
+The full bank/carrier records, original CIA routing package, payment/closure
+authorizations and complete drawing/expert exhibits remain unacquired in this
+pass. Another bank/telephone tranche already exists; it is preserved separately
+and its unfinished conclusions are not adopted here. No outreach, fees, filing,
+commit, push or new public publication occurred in this tranche.
+
+## Source conventions and provenance
+
+All PDF citations below use **one-based physical pages in the pinned acquired
+file**. Printed page numbers, ECF stamps, Bates identifiers and previous JSON
+locators are separate fields. A quoted party filing is evidence of that party's
+position, not an adjudicated historical fact. Repeated copies are not additional
+witnesses. The [source pins](source-pins.json), acquisition receipts and
+[claim/target ledger](findings.json) retain exact bytes, locators and limits.
+
+- **MFR:** [NARA media PDF](https://nara-media-001.s3.amazonaws.com/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00219.pdf),
+  six pages; SHA256 `56bca83074ff07e21a687f81799995a151ec9cdd2ce324f71c251ea55244bb07`.
+  Commons structured metadata identifies NARA2609810 and that media URL. The
+  NARA Catalog page was inaccessible through the web tool; its complete metadata
+  response was not acquired. NARA media and Commons PDF bytes match exactly.
+- **FBI2C5:** [FBI EO14040 section2(c), Part5](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file),
+  held official403-page release; specific pages14/15/89 checked.
+- **NOTES:** [official Commission notes PDF](https://www.9-11commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.pdf),
+  physical67-68, Chapter7 notes15-17 and25.
+- **D11180:** [official August28,2025 expert-review order](https://wp.nysd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2025-08/03-md-01570%2011180.pdf),
+  physical1,23-24, reviewing ECF10615 of December11,2024.
+- **D11182:** [official August28,2025 jurisdiction order](https://www.nysd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2025-08/03-md-01570%2011182.pdf),
+  physical28-29,41,45; previously held original, unchanged.
+- **P10199:** [plaintiffs' August2,2024 redacted averment](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/20240802%20Redacted%20public%20averment.pdf),
+  party-hosted primary filing copy, physical477-480; paragraphs1889-1908.
+- **K9795:** [Saudi Arabia's May10,2024 redacted reply](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/Docket%20%23%209795%20-%20Redacted%20Public%20Version%20%20KSA%20REPLY%20MOL%20ISO%20%5B9368%5D%20MTN%20to%20Dismiss%20%28Prev.%20filed%20under%20seal%20on%203.4%2C%202024%29.pdf),
+  party-hosted primary filing copy, physical48-49 / printed34-35.
+- **OIG:** [2005 ChapterV representation](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm),
+  III.A.4/6, III.B.3, notes130-135; [2006 representation](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/s0606/chapter5.htm)
+  was separately acquired. These are representations of the same oversight
+  chain, not independent witnesses or payment vouchers.
+
+## RF001: an underlying witness memorandum is now acquired
+
+The MFR is dated April20,2004 and identifies Team1A and its preparer. It is a
+staff memorandum of an interview, not a verbatim deposition transcript or audio
+recording. Its six physical pages were read and visually inspected in full.
+
+Physical4 records the following sequence: Bin Don and Bayoumi ordered food and
+sat waiting; Hazmi and Mihdhar entered speaking Arabic; Bayoumi addressed them
+and invited them to sit. It reports an invitation to San Diego, an apparent
+telephone-number exchange whose precise sequence the witness could not recall,
+and departure after about **thirty minutes**. It also records the witness's
+emphatic denial of advance information about the meeting and description of it
+as **purely a coincidence**. Both assistance-related observations and that
+contrary interpretation remain together.
+
+The MFR says his Arabic was **limited**, the exchange was vague to him, and
+Bayoumi sometimes translated. This qualifies use of him as an independent
+witness to the conversation's content. It does not permit either treating him
+as fluent or assuming that he understood no words whatsoever. Compare the
+2016 FBI summary's reported inability to understand Arabic, rather than silently
+choosing a language-proficiency description.
+
+The memoir-like interval and spoken recollections are not a calibrated record
+of minutes, advance knowledge or the conversation itself. The later two-minute
+account, thirty-minute accounts and the coincidence belief must not be merged.
+
+## RF002: the alias join is narrowed by explicit records
+
+The MFR physical1 names **Caysan Bin Don / Usama Dyson / Clayton Morgan**.
+FBI2C5 physical89, Bates **EO14040-002811**, explicitly associates **CAYSAN BIN
+DON / KAYSON BINDON DYSON / CLAYTON MORGAN** and the Los Angeles trip.
+Its physical14, Bates **EO14040-002736**, instead says **ISAMU DYSON (now known
+as CLAYTON BIN DON)**. These source wordings and spelling/name combinations
+remain distinct.
+
+This is direct documentary support for an alias relationship, not just a
+guess based on a similar story. It narrows the earlier source-identity gap.
+The exact crosswalk to the later **Kaysan Morgan** declaration/deposition still
+should be checked against the complete litigation documents. It does not
+create an additional witness, and name variants do not establish deception.
+No redacted identity, date of birth or personal contact detail was reconstructed.
+
+## RF003: earlier interview and sequence conflicts have exact targets
+
+The official NOTES physical67, Chapter7 notes15-17, identifies the
+**October8,2001 FBI interview of Isamu Dyson**, the April20,2004 Bin Don interview,
+and Bayoumi's October16-17,2003 interview. Note17 expressly describes a change
+between a recollection of prayer at the consulate before lunch plus one later
+mosque visit, and the later account of both prayer sessions at the mosque.
+The acquired MFR physical3-4 records mosque visits before and after the meal.
+The October2001 interview has not been acquired here, so that side is still
+known through the Commission's account of it.
+
+The MFR physical1-3 places the trip in **January2000**, without establishing a
+precise day. FBI2C5 physical14 says **approximately02/01/2000**. Neither is
+silently converted to the other. Recollection precision, interview prompting,
+calendar attribution and a substantive contradiction remain competing issues to
+test using the original interviews and dated travel records.
+
+These are specific consistency questions, not proof of a rehearsed story or an
+arranged attack-related meeting. The witness's own coincidence belief remains.
+
+## RF004: a camera-operator statement and a version-specific negative
+
+MFR physical5 says Bin Don filmed the apartment gathering at Bayoumi's request
+using Bayoumi's camera. It records that he was shown a tape and asked to identify
+people. It states that **Hazmi was not videotaped** and records the witness's
+later belief that Hazmi had asked not to be filmed. A witness belief about why
+someone is absent is not an observed instruction or a comprehensive media census.
+
+NOTES physical68, Chapter7 note25, likewise describes only Mihdhar appearing
+briefly on the FBI-provided video. This is related source use, not another
+independent camera record. The exact tape/file shown in2004, its duration and
+the relation to later claimed complete copies remain unknown. The full original
+video and Ex10K/10K-TR are still required. This statement does not establish that
+no other recording includes Hazmi, nor that the gathering was attack preparation.
+
+## RF005: the drawing now has a more precise custody and copy crosswalk
+
+D11182 physical28-29 identifies seven MPS copy pages, **Ex678M/MPS696_1-7**,
+an FBI copy **Ex679B/FBI1331-1337**, and a color-photo representation
+**Ex11N/MPS999x_X0417**, citing page5. It identifies the sketch at MPS696_4 and
+FBI1334. P10199 physical477 cites the color representation at page6, not5.
+These differing locators are retained; the actual exhibit editions have not
+been acquired, so the cause of the difference is untested.
+
+P10199 paragraphs1889-1896, physical477-478, alleges seizure on
+**September20,2001**, return of the original notebook on **May2,2002** under
+**Ex678DD / MPS2023-100 / FMT Receipt69/2002 / item32 / PSS/34**, and first
+inclusion of the sketch in FBI reporting in **March2012**, citing EO3659-3668
+and3965-3967. These are plaintiffs' attributed assertions supported by identified
+but unacquired underlying records. They are not independently verified dates of
+every agency's possession, knowledge, review or loss.
+
+The filing describes a commercial pad marked100 sheets while citing a
+seven-page copy set. The full notebook, used-page census and copying history
+are unknown;100 marketed sheets are not100 established written pages or93
+proved missing pages. These copy/custody identifiers make a finite retrieval
+request possible without claiming that the drawing was planted or concealed.
+
+## RF006: technical testimony, purpose and the court's own inference differ
+
+P10199 paragraphs1900-1908 describes Schiff's horizon/line-of-sight interpretation,
+pre-flight-planning use and an asserted relationship to50-70-mile calculations.
+K9795 physical48-49 argues that the equation is commonplace and undated, invokes
+Schiff deposition passages and **Moss report pp7,12-16**, and disputes the
+relationship to attack flight paths. Both are advocacy accounts. A quoted
+expert conclusion in a brief is not a new independent finding.
+
+The newly acquired D11180 physical23-24 upholds the treatment of both aviation
+experts. It accepts the construction of Moss's alternatives, describes Schiff
+as unqualified to testify about Bayoumi's relationship with the hijackers, and
+retains the reliability/helpfulness of his technical testimony subject to
+limitations including credibility commentary. It notes neither side objected
+to those portions of ECF10615. It does not exclude all of Schiff's testimony
+or adjudicate the mathematical interpretation as proving an attack plan.
+
+D11182 physical41 nevertheless makes a substantive preliminary inference about
+Bayoumi's knowledge from the drawing and other evidence; physical45 expressly
+leaves disputed meaning and credibility for merits determination. Judicial
+inference, expert admissibility, an engineering calculation and historical
+intent are different evidentiary propositions. Keeping all these records does
+not require treating them as logically incompatible or selecting a controlling
+historical explanation.
+
+Highest-value missing inputs: complete Ex678M,679B,11N,678DD; Schiff's Ex148
+and full Ex104 deposition; Moss's ECF9118-3 with exhibits; ECF10615; relevant
+underlying flight/visibility assumptions and independent dating/context. No
+flight-path or visibility reconstruction was performed in this pass.
+
+## RF007: CIA and informant purpose remain original-record gaps
+
+The newly retrieved2006 OIG chapter repeats the reported hold and payment chain;
+it is not the original CIR, an independent observation, or an actual voucher.
+The payment remains **$100,000 in July2003 with closure**, with no purpose
+established by the examined passage. The reported FBI noncomplicity finding,
+inconclusive polygraph and OIG interview limitations remain in the preceding
+study and are not displaced.
+
+The identified CIA accountability-report URL redirected to an HTML maintenance
+page instead of returning a PDF. Its saved response is marked non-PDF. That is
+an access result, not evidence of destruction, concealment or a changed CIA
+account. No original CIR/hold/access log, transmission receipt, response email,
+payment authorization, voucher or source-closure document was acquired. Search
+failure is bounded to this pass and does not establish nonexistence.
+
+## RF008: low-weight record/locator differences are preserved
+
+K9795 physical49 / printed35 says the restaurant was in **San Diego on a day
+trip from Los Angeles**, while its section heading concerns assistance in
+Los Angeles and the MFR identifies Culver City. That geographic wording is
+retained verbatim in the source; a clerical inversion is an untested possibility,
+not an adopted explanation. The sentence alone does not establish a second
+meeting, false testimony, or historical deception.
+
+The acquired P10199 PDF has **566 physical pages**, while an overlaid ECF10199
+stamp refers to567 and an older ECF9541 stamp uses566. Body-page numbers differ
+again. No missing-page finding follows without the complete docket versions.
+References above use the actual physical page and paragraph, not a blended
+pagination. The color-copy page5/page6 difference remains a separate exhibit
+locator question.
+
+The NARA media endpoint labels the MFR response **text/plain**, while its body
+has a PDF signature and matches the Commons PDF byte-for-byte. The supplied
+type and observed bytes are both preserved. This does not show a substantive
+change or deliberate substitution. These metadata/wording questions have much
+less bearing on attack participation than authenticated operational evidence.
+
+## Bundle status and next records
+
+| Requested bundle | Actual result here | Indispensable next input |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Bank/carrier originals | Existing separate tranche located and left unchanged; no completed original-record reconciliation adopted | Ex550/FBI8057; KSA Ex91/FBI2808-09; Ex12A and authenticated bank/carrier roots |
