+| Preserve conflicts, negative evidence and dependence | All RF records and findings.json | Coincidence belief, limited Arabic, source name/date variants, opposing expert accounts and scope limits retained. Several records repeat the same witness or exhibit. |
+| Explain precise remaining records | REPORT bundle table; targets.json | Requests have exhibit/Bates/date/paragraph targets and tests that could weaken as well as strengthen the hypotheses. No proposed retrieval is represented as done. |
+| Native/source preservation and revision diff | baseline.json; source-pins.json; diffs/ | Ten preceding artifacts pinned; source originals unchanged. New-document addition diff and separate native visual/hash verification recorded. |
+
+## Source and execution distinctions
+
+The research checkout is the existing isolated broader-evidence worktree. Current
+main workflow/storage/privacy controls were consulted. Existing public material
+is not promoted into case facts, pleadings or correspondence. The earlier Urban
+Moving publication is unrelated to these new artifacts and remains intact.
+
+The current source pass acquired9 responses in its initial receipt, including a
+six-page PDF through Commons. A later direct NARA media fetch acquired a second,
+byte-identical copy. A2006 OIG HTML representation and official25-page expert
+review order were acquired. CIA returned maintenance HTML, DPLA returned an
+empty entity, and the two transcribed-case mirror requests returned HTTP429.
+Those responses are preserved as access limits, not historical evidence of
+destruction or secrecy. No login, paywall or rate restriction was bypassed.
+
+Commons page wikitext contained only a metadata template; its structured data
+identified NARA2609810 and the actual media URL. The independent Catalog page
+was inaccessible in the web tool. The provenance claim is the observed direct
+byte match, not a claim that every catalog field was independently inspected.
+
+Initial source locators treated another study's JSON page values as zero-based.
+Direct PDF checks showed one-based values. Previously rendered pages remain;
+correct physical477 of P10199 and14/89 of FBI2C5 were added. The final report
+uses those actual pages. This is a documented correction to our locator use,
+not an alteration or adjudication of conflicting source records.
+
+Twenty-five native pages were rendered and actually inspected: all6 MFR pages,
+3 ECF11180 pages,4 ECF11182 pages,4 averment pages,2 reply pages,4 FBI release
+pages and2 Commission notes pages. Some initially selected pages supplied only
+context; all remain pinned. Rendering/inspection is separate from text extraction
+and the Git diff. No new PDF was authored, no mathematical reconstruction or
+historical-camera test was executed, and no full-case review is claimed.
+
